  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4df29301-9879-5cf1-ab82-1bc318554887" activityNameId="fa4be19c-a7bb-5a9e-a2d0-d6f946bdef2c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">All-in-one printer (WiFi), at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: All-in-one printer (WiFi), at plant
The dataset represents the typical all in one printers, with data sourced from literature and product sheets; UUID: c4a367d5-daf0-3660-85f1-ec052e12aabe
The dataset for this average inkjet printer are taken from the disassembly data from the inkjet all in one printer Kodak printer ESP7 (source: Babbitt et al., 2020) and the product sheets of printer manufacturers, i.e., HP, specifically HP OfficeJet Pro 9022e All-in-One Printer (HP, 2023). The key technical specifications are built-in WiFi connectivity, 1 GHz processor, 512 MB memory, and 4 inkjet cartridges. The total weight of the printer is approximately 11.6 kg, which includes the casing materials (plastics, aluminum, steel, and glass), cartridges, and electronics such as printed circuit boards.
Location: Data for global average all in one printers.
Technology: Average all in one printers with WiFi connection.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: Average technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c4a367d5-daf0-3660-85f1-ec052e12aabe.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
